{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-20-1","title":"Jeremiah 20:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Pashur, smiting Jeremiah, receives a new name, and a fearful doom. 7 Jeremiah complains of contempt; 10 of treachery; 14 and of his birth.</p>\n<p>Immer. 1Ch 24:14; Ezr 2:37,38; Ne 7:40,41 chief. 2Ki 25:18; 2Ch 35:8; Ac 4:1; 5:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-2","title":"Jeremiah 20:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>smote. 1:19; 19:14,15; 26:8; 29:26; 36:26; 37:15,16; 38:6; 1Ki 22:27 2Ch 16:10; 24:21; Am 7:10-13; Mt 5:10-12; 21:35; 23:34-37; Ac 4:3 Ac 5:18,40; 7:52; 16:22-24; Heb 11:36,37; Re 2:10; 17:6 the stocks.{Hammahpecheth,} from {haphach,} \"to overturn, subvert, distort,\" generally denotes an overthrow, (De 29:22. Isa 1:7; 10:19,) and seems to signify here a sort of stocks, by which the limbs were distorted into uneasy postures. So the Chaldee, {keephtha} and Jerome, {nervus,} which he explains in his comment as \"a kind of wooden fetter, into which the feet were thrust, {vinculi lignei genus, cui pedes inseruntur.} Some learned men understand it as merely signifying a place of confinement, or house of correction; but the word is never used for any of the prisons into which the prophet was afterwards cast; and the punishment seems to have been public and ignominious.</p>\n<p>in the high. 37:13; 38:7; Zec 14:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-3","title":"Jeremiah 20:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Pashur. Ac 4:5-7; 16:30,35-39 hath. 7:32; 19:2,6; Ge 17:5,15; 32:28; Isa 8:3; Ho 1:4-9 Magor-missabib. this is, Fear round about. 10; 6:25; 46:5; 29:29; Ps 31:13; La 2:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-4","title":"Jeremiah 20:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>I will make. De 28:65-67; Job 18:11-21; 20:23-26; Ps 73:19; Eze 26:17-21 Mt 27:4,5 thine. 29:21; 39:6,7; De 28:32-34; 1Sa 2:33; 2Ki 25:7 I will give. 19:15; 21:4-10; 25:9; 32:27-31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-5","title":"Jeremiah 20:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>I will deliver. 3:24; 4:20; 12:12; 15:13; 24:8-10; 27:19-22; 32:3-5; 39:2,8; 52:7-23 2Ki 20:17,18; 24:12-16; 25:13-17; 2Ch 36:10,17-19; La 1:7,10 La 4:12; Eze 22:25; Da 1:2 labours.The word labours is here used for the produce of labour.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-6","title":"Jeremiah 20:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>thou. Pashur. 28:15-17; 29:21,22,32; Ac 13:8-11 thy friends. 4; 5:31; 6:13-15; 8:10,11; 14:14,15; 23:14-17,25,26,32 Isa 9:15; La 2:14; Eze 13:4-16,22,23; 22:28; Mic 2:11; Zec 13:3 2Pe 2:1-3 thou hast. Le 26:17; De 28:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-7","title":"Jeremiah 20:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>deceived. or, enticed. 1:6-8,18,19; 15:18; 17:16; Ex 5:22,23; Nu 11:11-15 thou art. 9; Eze 3:14; Mic 3:8; 1Co 9:6 I am. 15:10; 29:26; 2Ki 2:23; Ps 22:6,7; 35:15,16; 69:9-12; La 3:14 Ho 9:7; Lu 16:14; 22:63,64; 23:11,35,36; Ac 17:18,32; 1Co 4:9-13 Heb 11:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-8","title":"Jeremiah 20:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>I cried. 4:19-22; 5:1,6,15-17; 6:6,7; 7:9; 13:13,14; 15:1-4,13,14; 17:27 18:16,17; 19:7-11; 28:8 the word. 7; 6:10; 2Ch 36:16; La 3:61-63; Lu 11:45; Heb 11:26; 13:13; 1Pe 4:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-9","title":"Jeremiah 20:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>I will. 1Ki 19:3,4; Joh 1:2,3; 4:2,3; Lu 9:62; Ac 15:37,38 was in. 6:11; Job 32:18-20; Ps 39:3; Eze 3:14; Ac 4:20; 17:16; 18:5 1Co 9:16,17; 2Co 5:13-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-10","title":"Jeremiah 20:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>I heard. Ps 31:13; 57:4; 64:2-4; Mt 26:59,60 fear. 3 Report. 18:18; Ne 6:6-13; Pr 10:18; Isa 29:21; Eze 22:9; Lu 20:20 Ac 6:11-15; 24:1-9,13 All my familiars. Heb. Every man of my peace. Job 19:19; Ps 41:9; 55:13,14; Lu 11:53,54; 12:52,53 we shall. 1Ki 19:2; 21:20; 22:8,27; Mr 6:19-28; Ac 5:33; 7:54; 23:12-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-11","title":"Jeremiah 20:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>the Lord. 1:8,19; 15:20; Isa 41:10,14; Ro 8:31; 2Ti 4:17 a mighty. Ps 47:2; 65:5; 66:5 my. 17:18; De 32:35,36; Ps 27:1,2; Joh 18:4-6 and they. 1:19; 15:20 everlasting. 23:40; Ps 6:10; 35:26; 40:14; Isa 45:16; Da 12:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-12","title":"Jeremiah 20:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>that. 17:10; Ps 7:9; 11:5; 17:3; 26:2,3; 139:23; Re 2:23 let me. 11:20; 12:8; 17:18; 18:19-23; 2Ch 24:22; Ps 54:7; 59:10; 109:6-20 Re 6:10; 18:20; 19:2,3 for. 1Sa 1:15; Ps 62:8; 86:4; Isa 37:14; 38:14; 1Pe 2:23; 4:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-13","title":"Jeremiah 20:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>for. Ps 34:6; 35:9-11; 69:33; 72:4; 109:30,31; Isa 25:4; Jas 2:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-14","title":"Jeremiah 20:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>15:10; Job 3:3-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-15","title":"Jeremiah 20:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>A man. 1:5; Ge 21:5,6; Lu 1:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-16","title":"Jeremiah 20:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>as. Ge 19:24,25; De 29:23; Ho 11:8; Am 4:11; Zep 2:9; Lu 17:29; 2Pe 2:6 Jude 1:7 repented. 18:8; 26:13; Jon 3:4,9,10; 4:2 let him. 4:19; 18:22; 48:3,4; Eze 21:22; Ho 10:14; Am 1:14; 2:2; Zep 1:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-17","title":"Jeremiah 20:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>he slew. Job 3:10,11,16; 10:18,19; Ec 6:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-20-18","title":"Jeremiah 20:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>came. Job 3:20; 14:1,13; La 3:1 to see. 8:18; Ge 3:16-19; Ps 90:10; La 1:12; Joh 16:20; Heb 10:36 with. Ps 69:19; Isa 1:6; 51:7; Ac 5:41; 1Co 4:9-13; 2Ti 1:12; Heb 11:36 Heb 12:2; 13:13; 1Pe 4:14-16</p>"}]}